<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<!--
		Probe GI: the CPU baker with its own BVH, the GPU round path, the scene acceleration
		structure and the debug rendering of probes.

		This used to live in DecaEngine.Editor - four and a half thousand lines of runtime among the
		ImGui windows. Nothing about it is editor-specific: the baker is called by the model preview,
		by the scene viewport and by the headless probes, and tomorrow it will be called by the game.
		The flip side of the same thing: testing the ray fan math meant dragging the entire editor
		into the test project.

		The dependency on Graphics.Diligent is deliberate and temporary: the GPU path (ProbeRoundGpu,
		ProbeRoundPipelines, ProbeSceneAccel) talks to DiligentGraphicsApi directly, because
		IGraphicsApi simply has no compute pipelines or acceleration structures. It will go away once
		the abstractions catch up.
	-->
	<ItemGroup>
		<ProjectReference Include="..\DecaEngine.Core\DecaEngine.Core.csproj" />
		<ProjectReference Include="..\DecaEngine.Graphics.Core\DecaEngine.Graphics.Core.csproj" />
		<ProjectReference Include="..\DecaEngine.Graphics.Diligent\DecaEngine.Graphics.Diligent.csproj" />
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
